{
  "version": 1,
  "note": "The cross-backend projection contract. Rust checks it in longhorn-poodle; TypeScript checks it in longhorn-poodle-svelte. Either side drifting fails its own gate. Hand-written on purpose: the point is that two independent implementations agree, so neither generates the other. See card 171 and memo 022.",
